#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56caab23-f54d-58ee-99db-99c651f78e5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circulation of a Vector Field Over a Region Containing Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc41a40b-917a-57ad-93c5-f9db0205c2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130746} {:answer/id #uuid "34e14694-9434-5ad9-aa2d-2969b9ae1cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130747} {:answer/id #uuid "4b2ce2f4-0374-5148-947b-96f3d8b6b4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130748} {:answer/id #uuid "5d7d99a7-294b-5cf9-90af-ed4075071bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130749} {:answer/id #uuid "323a1bfd-c415-5a52-8f82-c95d150e0d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e14694-9434-5ad9-aa2d-2969b9ae1cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130747} :answer-field/id #uuid "59065be7-12d4-5585-856f-70e63556d4de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa43bdf8-83a8-50c7-a713-6a675dec7cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-126558" :question/problem "![](images/72/7264984a1c19c247c030feae04615bb0c46205ca70475db1240db964ad6007b2.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=10,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-4,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/0d/0de833fcc39b6295418c1558cf1187774db7b4ada1d697f2dcac8c35858563df.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =10-4-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56caab23-f54d-58ee-99db-99c651f78e5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circulation of a Vector Field Over a Region Containing Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a658638-403e-5ab9-a8f1-33237b22ab86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497887} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5743a8-8fd6-5394-b293-eb9fd93fef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497979} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9eb833-f8ff-5a68-9ca4-2b64e1730af